From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:32:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] HTMLMediaElement: a local video file's Swap Eyes
 correction

A person who corrects a file whose mark has its eyes the wrong way round
stores the correction with the file: the extended attribute
user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes, which libstereo-policy reads and writes,
and which copies and moves that keep extended attributes keep (Dolphin
and the edition's other programs use it).

A video loaded from a file: URI now takes that correction as its Swap
Eyes. Content processes cannot read extended attributes, so the file
content process asks the parent process (PContent.GetStereoFileSwap),
which answers only that process, only for a file: URI, and reads the
attribute away from its main thread. The answer applies only if the
element still loads that file. The 3D Video menu's Swap Eyes then shows
it, and the viewer may turn it off for this playback.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
